<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zulu Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zulu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zulu Kingdom was a powerful state in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> built by Shaka from the 1810s onward through military reform and conquest. Its rise was associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a>, a period of warfare and migration that spread across southern Africa. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> record that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni-speaking</a> groups displaced by these upheavals invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> and destroyed the Rozvi state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom.jpg" alt="Zulu Kingdom" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seb az86556 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LocationZululandca1890.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
